      "content": "Ah, the quest for error handling, a noble endeavor indeed! Let's fortify your macro with the protective enchantments of VBA's error handling. This way, if the goblins of error sneak up on your macro, it won't be caught off guard and will instead handle the situation with the grace of a seasoned adventurer.\n\nHere's how you can add error handling to your macro:\n\n```vba\nSub MonthlyRecon()\n    On Error GoTo ErrorHandler\n    Dim ws As Worksheet\n    Set ws = ThisWorkbook.Sheets(\"Reconciliation_Report\")\n    ws.Range(\"A1\").Value = \"Monthly Summary\"\n    ws.Range(\"A1\").Select\n    ws.Range(\"B2:Z100\").Font.Bold = True\n    Exit Sub\n\nErrorHandler:\n    MsgBox \"An error occurred: \" & Err.Description, vbCritical, \"Error in MonthlyRecon\"\nEnd Sub\n```\n\nWith this spell in place, if the goblins of error do appear, your macro will not crash. Instead, it will display a message box with the error description, allowing you to investigate the issue further. Remember, even the most seasoned adventurers encounter goblins along their journey, but it's how you handle them that defines your success.",
